{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q010_rossmann_family_function_divergence","answer":"In public SCOPe release 2.08, these are three distinct families: alcohol-dehydrogenase-like C-terminal domains (SUNID 51736; c.2.1.1), CoA-binding domains (SUNID 51900; c.2.1.8), and potassium-channel NAD-binding domains (SUNID 63944; c.2.1.9). All descend from the same NAD(P)-binding Rossmann-fold superfamily (SUNID 51735; c.2.1), within the same Rossmann fold (SUNID 51734; c.2) and alpha/beta class (c). Sharing a superfamily is stronger than merely sharing a fold: SCOPe treats remote common ancestry as probable. Their placement in different families, however, reflects substantial divergence and does not imply close sequence similarity or interchangeable biological roles.

Accordingly, one must not transfer alcohol-dehydrogenase activity, CoA specificity, NAD binding, catalytic residues, or potassium-channel regulation among these families from the classification alone. The potassium-channel entry describes a soluble channel-associated regulatory domain, not the membrane pore, and its historical family name does not prove that every member binds NAD physiologically. Likewise, the CoA-binding family label is not a general annotation for all CoA-binding proteins.

A structure from another c.2.1 family can be a remote template for the conserved Rossmann-like core, but domain boundaries, alignment, insertions, ligand pocket, catalytic geometry, oligomeric context, and multidomain architecture require independent validation. Prefer representatives from the same family and with the closest sequence, matching construct and ligand state; use multiple superfamily-level representatives if no same-family template exists rather than treating one representative as interchangeable across c.2.1. Functional transfer should additionally require family-specific sequence/structure evidence and biochemical evidence such as ligand-binding, enzymology, or channel-regulation measurements.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info — /api/v1/; /api/v1/releases/current","mcp__scope__search_scop — used to locate the public SUNIDs and SCCS identifiers","mcp__scope__get_scop_node — /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944/parents"]}]}
